  "prefLabel": "Rev 501.03 Excavation",
  "priorExpiration": "2011-03-31",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 501.03 \"Excavation\" means “excavation” as defined in RSA 155-E:1, II namely “a land area which is used, or has been used, for the commercial taking of earth, including all slopes.” Excavation does not include any site of an excavation which ceased commercially useful operation prior to August 24, 1977, or any reclaimed area.\n\nSource. #7381, eff 10-24-00; ss by #7860, eff 3-31-03, EXPIRED: 3-31-11\n\nNew. #9926, eff 5-18-11 (from Rev 501.02); ss by #12834, eff 7-25-19",
